1
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:31,640
Don't chase after things
beyond your reach.

2
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:33,200
If I step back now,

3
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,200
I'll never be good enough for Fon

4
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:38,160
in her father's eyes.

5
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:40,360
Just be good to Fon

6
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:42,320
and make her happy.

7
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,560
I think that's enough.

8
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:47,800
I've hired professionals
to take care of Oab's woman.

9
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,960
Mom, wake up.

10
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,080
It has to be Peng.

11
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,880
Can we end this here?

12
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:03,320
After the funeral, we'll tell the chief
that we're quitting.

13
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:07,200
I'm sorry this all happened to you
because of me.

14
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,600
You guys were arrested

15
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,800
for murder.
Aren't you going to name names?

16
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:15,400
- No.
- If you can do what you say,

17
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:16,720
you'll be out sooner than you think.

18
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:35,360
Thank you so much

19
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:37,520
for moving here to stay at this temple.

20
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,000
If there's anything you need,
please let me know.

21
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:42,240
I'm only worried about Dom.

22
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:45,600
He'll have to adjust to living here.

23
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,200
He doesn't have any friends.

24
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,400
Hello, Aunt Sook.

25
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:58,840
How are you, Dom? I brought you something.

26
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:01,760
Here, I made some extra for you.

27
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,800
Thank you.

28
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:06,800
I'll put Grandpa Monk's meal on a plate
so you can bring it for the noon offering.

29
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:07,840
Okay.

30
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:09,720
Here you go.

31
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:16,120
Fon, go help set out the food
for the monk's noon offering.

32
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:17,720
Okay, Mom.

33
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:21,480
How are you doing, Dom? Look at you.

34
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:24,040
You're so small,
and you're fighting already?

35
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,920
I won, Auntie.

36
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,480
I even made a hundred baht.

37
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:30,880
But was it really worth it?

38
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:34,560
- Fon.
- I'm coming, Mom.

39
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:36,760
What took you so long? Give it here.

40
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:40,000
Put some balm on it. Look at you.

41
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:42,640
How is it?

42
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:45,920
It hurts, doesn't it? Let me see.

43
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,120
Your whole face is bruised.

44
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:53,080
I never approved of you two
from the start.

45
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:58,480
Now you're talking about getting married?
I don't think you're ready.

46
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:14,200
I know you truly love Fon.

47
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:18,320
Just take good care of her, love her,

48
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,959
and build your life together step by step.

49
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:50,640
Those two
confessed to everything themselves.

50
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,640
They didn't give up any names

51
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:56,360
and said nobody hired them.

52
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:59,440
The interrogation was useless.

53
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:11,800
Fon.

54
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:16,840
I don't think you can stay here anymore.

55
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:21,240
Stay at my place for now.
You'll be safer there.

56
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:25,240
I'm not leaving.
If they want me, they can come.

57
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:29,000
You can't keep putting your life
at risk like this.

58
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:36,560
Your life means too much to me.

59
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,640
You're taking the bag too?

60
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,640
It's Fon's.

61
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,240
I asked her to stay at my place.

62
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:04,040
It's safer this way.

63
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,600
Come on.

64
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:52,000
Thank you.

65
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,440
I brought your friend here for you.

66
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,560
Are you okay here?

67
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:45,000
Did you call your dad yet?

68
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:53,280
I don't know how to start.

69
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,000
Dad's going to be so hurt.

70
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,960
Sooner or later,
Uncle Chai will find out anyway.

71
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:33,160
It's better he hears it from you…

72
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,920
than someone else.

73
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:43,360
Okay?

74
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,680
Want me to stay with you?

75
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,120
Dad.

76
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:07,800
Mom's not here anymore.

77
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:12,520
SIAM BOXING

78
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:17,880
Hey, Dom. What happened?

79
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,200
You already heard?

80
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:23,040
Everyone at the camp knows.

81
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:25,280
I bet it was Peng's men again.

82
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,240
Probably.

83
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:32,840
That's just cowardly,
going after a woman like that.

84
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:40,800
And how's Fon doing?

85
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:50,320
What are they doing about the funeral?

86
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:54,400
Tomorrow we'll pick up the body
and take her to Khon Kaen.

87
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:55,600
Are you going with her?

88
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,320
Things are dangerous like this.

89
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:03,000
You've gotta watch your back all the time.

90
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:05,040
Going anywhere alone is risky.

91
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:07,680
I'd say going home, finding a wife,
and living a simple life

92
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:09,680
in the countryside would be easier.

93
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:21,480
You're going with Dom alone?

94
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:25,040
After what happened,
shouldn't you be more careful?

95
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:28,240
They just made their move,
and their men got arrested.

96
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:32,200
They'll be careful.
They won't make a move right now.

97
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:36,200
I don't want to clean up your mess
like last time.

98
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:43,280
I want her to go with people she trusts.
She'll feel better.

99
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:47,000
Just have our men ready here.

100
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:50,680
I should be back
around Arm's death anniversary.

101
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:54,520
Getting the men ready isn't a problem.

102
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:57,560
You just take care of yourself.
Drive safely.

103
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:05,520
MORTUARY

104
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:20,760
Thank you for everything, Mom.

105
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:26,880
<i>Thank you for believing in me,</i>

106
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:29,640
<i>for treating me like your own son,</i>

107
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:32,920
<i>and for seeing the worth</i>
<i>in a temple boy like me.</i>

108
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:38,800
I promise you, Mom.

109
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:41,920
I'll protect Fon

110
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,160
with my life.

111
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:24,400
The hearse is in front of the hospital.
I'll go with Fon.

112
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:26,160
You just follow behind us.

113
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:38,400
Mom.

114
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:29,240
Why are you sitting here alone?

115
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:38,280
I think I'll go back to Khon Kaen.

116
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:40,720
Why?

117
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:42,720
I wanted to be a boxer.

118
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,080
But lately,

119
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,080
I've held a gun
more than I've worn gloves.

120
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:55,440
It's like this at first.

121
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:57,640
You'll get used to it.

122
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,680
I don't think I ever will.

123
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,360
I don't want you to quit.

124
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:17,600
I don't want to lose
a good person like you.

125
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:21,560
If you really want to box,

126
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:23,840
I'll find you a fight.

127
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:29,000
What do you want?

128
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:32,400
Money, power.

129
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:34,760
Women.

130
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:37,200
I can get you anything.

131
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:44,080
I used to want money.

132
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,920
I wanted security in life.

133
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:49,800
But now,

134
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:52,200
I think I don't need to have
a lot of money.

135
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,080
If I work hard,

136
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,840
I can still have a good life.

137
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:01,400
Build a family.

138
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:04,480
Live without fear with the people I love.

139
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:08,920
That's enough for me.

140
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:12,680
I won't let you quit.

141
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:19,520
In my world, a true friend

142
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,360
is worth more than money.

143
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:29,000
You proved you're a real friend.

144
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:32,840
I can put my life in your hands.

145
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,360
Thank you for coming.

146
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:19,720
Dad.

147
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:25,400
Don't cry. You'll make Mom worry.

148
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:31,360
Mom.

149
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:34,720
Don't worry.

150
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:37,720
I'll take care of Dad.

151
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:41,160
Once I'm done with everything in Bangkok,

152
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:45,680
I'll move back to Khon Kaen
and live with Dad.

153
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:52,600
Rest peacefully, Mom.

154
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:58,240
Keep blessing us from above, okay?

155
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:06,520
Don't cry.

156
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:23,200
Uncle Chai, Dom volunteered
to stay and keep watch tonight.

157
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:29,160
You and Fon go home first.

158
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,760
I'll help Dom close up the hall.

159
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:33,640
Yes.

160
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,120
Come on.

161
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:00,720
I'm sorry, Dad.

162
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:12,360
This is because of you.

163
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:16,200
You dragged my family into danger.

164
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,280
My wife died

165
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:23,080
because of your foolish decisions.

166
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:29,720
Sook loved you so much.

167
00:22:30,360 --> 00:22:32,800
She stood by you. She believed in you.

168
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:34,720
And look what happened.

169
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:37,560
She's lying in a coffin now.

170
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:39,680
Do you see what happens

171
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:43,480
to the people who love you?

172
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:45,400
What they get for protecting you?

173
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:50,200
Please.

174
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:54,080
Leave my family alone.

175
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:56,000
I'm begging you.

176
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,400
Fon.

177
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:27,120
I understand.

178
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:31,920
I've lost someone I loved too.

179
00:23:37,160 --> 00:23:38,560
I know what this feels like.

180
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,480
I miss her all the time.

181
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:46,120
But she'll never truly be gone.

182
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:56,960
It'll get better, Fon.

183
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:01,400
Not because

184
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:03,840
we forget them.

185
00:24:07,760 --> 00:24:08,840
But because

186
00:24:10,800 --> 00:24:12,680
we slowly get used to

187
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:17,000
what it feels like without them.

188
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:22,560
They never really leave us.

189
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:34,360
I'm sorry.

190
00:24:41,760 --> 00:24:43,040
I promise

191
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:48,480
I'll take responsibility
for what happened to your mom

192
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:50,800
and your family.

193
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:15,480
TONGSOOK SAISOMBAT

194
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:31,600
Mom.

195
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:35,600
I shouldn't have chosen this path.

196
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:57,800
It's been a long time
since you came to the temple.

197
00:26:00,680 --> 00:26:01,920
Yes, Grandpa Monk.

198
00:26:03,080 --> 00:26:05,960
I was working in Bangkok.

199
00:26:06,040 --> 00:26:08,360
Sook told me about it before.

200
00:26:08,440 --> 00:26:10,800
You must be feeling troubled.

201
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:16,760
Yes.

202
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:23,320
I want to leave the job I'm doing.

203
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:25,960
But my boss

204
00:26:27,440 --> 00:26:28,640
won't let me quit.

205
00:26:30,280 --> 00:26:33,400
He says he trusts me and believes in me.

206
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:35,440
And what do you think?

207
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:40,160
I don't know…

208
00:26:42,600 --> 00:26:44,200
Everything

209
00:26:44,280 --> 00:26:47,240
in life is our own choice.

210
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:50,440
If you don't want to do something

211
00:26:50,520 --> 00:26:54,280
and choose to leave, no one can stop you.

212
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:57,160
Unless,

213
00:26:57,800 --> 00:27:00,600
deep down, you still want to stay.

214
00:27:02,600 --> 00:27:04,720
Dom, think about it.

215
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:09,160
Once you find your answer,
making your decision will become easier.

216
00:27:25,320 --> 00:27:27,840
I got home last night,
and you're already waiting?

217
00:27:31,280 --> 00:27:33,000
How's Fon doing?

218
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:35,200
She's getting better.

219
00:27:35,280 --> 00:27:38,640
She's getting some rest.
The funeral must've been exhausting.

220
00:27:41,320 --> 00:27:42,400
What's up? Why wait for me?

221
00:27:43,800 --> 00:27:45,240
I got word

222
00:27:45,880 --> 00:27:48,040
that Peng wants the promoter
to find a fighter for Man.

223
00:27:49,280 --> 00:27:50,480
Which promoter?

224
00:27:50,560 --> 00:27:52,120
Boss Jong.

225
00:27:57,120 --> 00:27:59,640
I heard you're looking for
an opponent for Man.

226
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:06,160
Peng wants Man to fight for the belt.

227
00:28:06,760 --> 00:28:07,840
It's been vacant for a year.

228
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:14,760
Boss.

229
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:18,360
Can you let my guy fight in this match?

230
00:28:22,800 --> 00:28:25,000
Don't joke around with me like that.

231
00:28:28,200 --> 00:28:30,120
This belt used to belong to my camp

232
00:28:31,160 --> 00:28:33,280
before my fighter died.

233
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:38,360
My camp should have the right to it first,
don't you think?

234
00:28:41,240 --> 00:28:46,760
The problem is, King Boxing Camp
doesn't have any famous fighters.

235
00:28:47,880 --> 00:28:50,600
If I'm going to organize
a big match and draw a crowd,

236
00:28:51,120 --> 00:28:53,560
the fighters need to have a name.

237
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:57,280
Otherwise, I can't sell it.
The boxing fans won't show up.

238
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:05,000
How much do you think

239
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:07,920
you can make from this fight?

240
00:29:09,400 --> 00:29:11,400
Fight against Oab's King Camp?

241
00:29:12,160 --> 00:29:14,560
The belt used to belong to his camp.

242
00:29:15,200 --> 00:29:18,480
If there's going to be a title fight,
they should get the first shot.

243
00:29:19,120 --> 00:29:21,600
Who's he gonna send?
Does he even have any skilled fighters?

244
00:29:22,760 --> 00:29:24,280
All he has are debt collectors.

245
00:29:24,840 --> 00:29:28,080
If Oab gives me a name, I'll let you know.

246
00:29:29,560 --> 00:29:30,720
I'm leaving.

247
00:29:36,040 --> 00:29:37,800
Who do you think he'll send, Liang?

248
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:07,240
Training late, huh?

249
00:30:10,040 --> 00:30:11,160
Here.

250
00:30:17,520 --> 00:30:19,080
How can you stand seeing all this?

251
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:22,720
After seeing Fon's mom die,

252
00:30:23,320 --> 00:30:24,360
I already wanted to quit.

253
00:30:30,280 --> 00:30:33,320
Just because I keep going
doesn't mean I can take it.

254
00:30:45,840 --> 00:30:46,720
This place…

255
00:30:50,320 --> 00:30:51,880
was my little brother's dream.

256
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:57,240
A dream I made come true.

257
00:30:59,880 --> 00:31:03,120
But in the end,
he wasn't here to enjoy it.

258
00:31:06,480 --> 00:31:07,960
Do you think that doesn't hurt me?

259
00:31:15,920 --> 00:31:17,640
I have to keep living

260
00:31:18,520 --> 00:31:21,280
so I can see the person who hurt me

261
00:31:22,600 --> 00:31:24,360
suffer a hundred times more.

262
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:45,360
Dom.

263
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:48,800
Wake up.

264
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:57,240
- What time is it?
- It's eight.

265
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:01,480
Everyone's back from their run.

266
00:32:01,560 --> 00:32:03,640
Why didn't you wake me up?

267
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:06,400
I tried, but you wouldn't wake up.

268
00:32:08,080 --> 00:32:12,040
Hey, Oab said you don't need to help
at the office anymore.

269
00:32:12,840 --> 00:32:13,800
Why?

270
00:32:13,880 --> 00:32:17,480
He wants you to stay and train here
unless he needs you.

271
00:32:29,120 --> 00:32:30,440
Dom.

272
00:32:31,200 --> 00:32:32,520
Get in the ring with me.

273
00:32:49,120 --> 00:32:52,680
You stopped me from helping at the office
because you wanted me to train?

274
00:32:54,360 --> 00:32:55,560
Yeah.

275
00:32:56,520 --> 00:32:58,320
From now on,
you're training with me every day.

276
00:33:00,520 --> 00:33:01,720
In a month,

277
00:33:02,920 --> 00:33:04,120
I'll have you fight Man.

278
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:09,360
Man Ocean?

279
00:33:10,640 --> 00:33:13,160
Yeah. I already talked to the promoter.

280
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:15,200
Didn't you say you wanted to box?

281
00:33:19,520 --> 00:33:20,840
But I already asked to quit.

282
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:23,080
That's why I'm giving you this
in exchange.

283
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:26,320
Can you not quit?

284
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:31,600
I'll get you a fight at Lumpinee.

285
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:40,880
I've never fought before.

286
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:43,600
Would they really
let me fight at Lumpinee?

287
00:33:43,680 --> 00:33:45,120
You're in my camp, aren't you?

288
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:50,480
Even if you've never boxed once,

289
00:33:51,480 --> 00:33:52,840
I can get you into Lumpinee.

290
00:34:13,960 --> 00:34:14,960
Fon.

291
00:34:19,199 --> 00:34:20,600
I'm sorry about your mom.

292
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:25,080
Thank you.

293
00:34:25,679 --> 00:34:28,400
But they're saying the same thing
I told you on the phone.

294
00:34:28,480 --> 00:34:31,360
They're lying.
Aren't you going to investigate further?

295
00:34:33,480 --> 00:34:36,679
How can I? They didn't name anyone.

296
00:34:38,880 --> 00:34:40,840
But I've never met them before in my life.

297
00:34:41,760 --> 00:34:45,239
What did I do to make them hate me
enough to kill me?

298
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:46,560
I don't know.

299
00:34:52,760 --> 00:34:53,880
Champ.

300
00:34:59,520 --> 00:35:01,240
Can we go somewhere quiet
and talk for a bit?

301
00:35:01,880 --> 00:35:03,080
About what?

302
00:35:04,160 --> 00:35:05,040
About Dom.

303
00:35:15,600 --> 00:35:16,440
What is it?

304
00:35:19,920 --> 00:35:21,520
Dom and I want to withdraw.

305
00:35:22,920 --> 00:35:25,360
I wanted to tell you first.
Dom will probably tell you himself.

306
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:33,600
We can't do this anymore.
They tried to kill me.

307
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:37,320
And my mom ended up dying because of this.

308
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:46,680
I'll talk to the chief first.

309
00:35:54,960 --> 00:35:55,680
ADMINISTRATION

310
00:35:58,160 --> 00:35:59,000
Fon.

311
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:02,280
I'm sorry about your mom.

312
00:36:04,880 --> 00:36:05,720
Thanks.

313
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:09,680
When I heard you were back at work,
I rushed over to see you.

314
00:36:09,760 --> 00:36:12,040
I'm sorry
I couldn't make it to the funeral.

315
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:15,920
Khon Kaen is pretty far.
It's okay, I understand.

316
00:36:20,960 --> 00:36:24,400
Besides apologizing,
there's something else I need to tell you.

317
00:36:30,360 --> 00:36:32,240
Do you remember when that car hit you?

318
00:36:33,320 --> 00:36:34,360
Someone died.

319
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:36,520
They worked for Peng, a powerful figure.

320
00:36:36,600 --> 00:36:38,960
I think it's connected to your case.

321
00:36:43,520 --> 00:36:44,760
Did they catch who did it?

322
00:36:45,840 --> 00:36:49,240
From the cases I've read
involving powerful people,

323
00:36:49,320 --> 00:36:53,080
they almost never catch the real culprit.
If they do, it's usually just a scapegoat.

324
00:37:09,200 --> 00:37:10,280
Dom.

325
00:37:12,280 --> 00:37:13,320
Waiting for Oab?

326
00:37:14,480 --> 00:37:15,680
Does anyone know you're here?

327
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:18,400
He told me to bring the stuff here first.

328
00:37:21,720 --> 00:37:24,600
I already talked to Oab about quitting
and moving back to Khon Kaen.

329
00:37:33,560 --> 00:37:35,160
But he won't let me leave.

330
00:37:36,840 --> 00:37:38,360
If he won't let you quit, that's on him.

331
00:37:39,200 --> 00:37:42,000
But if you want to leave,
that's your choice.

332
00:37:44,960 --> 00:37:46,920
He's letting me fight Man Ocean

333
00:37:47,520 --> 00:37:49,080
at Lumpinee.

334
00:37:49,160 --> 00:37:50,440
Dom.

335
00:37:50,520 --> 00:37:52,800
He already talked to the promoter.

336
00:37:52,880 --> 00:37:55,360
If I don't fight,
he'll be in a lot of trouble.

337
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:58,960
You changed your mind
because of this, didn't you?

338
00:38:00,920 --> 00:38:02,360
Didn't you tell me before

339
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:05,080
that if you had to choose
between me and boxing,

340
00:38:05,800 --> 00:38:07,160
you'd choose me?

341
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:21,800
Dom.

342
00:38:26,600 --> 00:38:27,680
I want to choose you too.

343
00:38:29,320 --> 00:38:31,720
But with everything happening now,
I can't do that.

344
00:38:33,120 --> 00:38:34,400
What situation?

345
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:37,040
And if you wait any longer,

346
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:39,760
will it become impossible for you
to walk away?

347
00:38:41,640 --> 00:38:43,280
Is it really because of the situation

348
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:46,800
or because deep down
you don't want to leave?

349
00:38:47,800 --> 00:38:49,080
I want to leave.

350
00:38:50,480 --> 00:38:53,280
I don't want you
to be with another man who isn't me.

351
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:57,720
And I don't want anyone else to die
because of my decisions.

352
00:39:00,680 --> 00:39:01,960
But I don't know

353
00:39:02,040 --> 00:39:04,880
if I'll ever get another chance
to fight at Lumpinee again.

354
00:39:16,680 --> 00:39:17,680
I'm sorry.

355
00:39:19,720 --> 00:39:20,920
I'm really sorry.

356
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,920
If you have to fight this time,

357
00:39:40,760 --> 00:39:41,800
it's okay.

358
00:39:44,240 --> 00:39:45,840
Do what you need to do and finish it.

359
00:39:51,840 --> 00:39:55,000
When it's over, let's go home.

360
00:39:56,920 --> 00:39:59,320
I'll move back to Khon Kaen too.

361
00:40:51,160 --> 00:40:52,080
Dom.

362
00:40:53,840 --> 00:40:55,240
Aren't you happy?

363
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:58,200
It's Lumpinee, man!

364
00:40:58,840 --> 00:41:01,680
If it were me, I wouldn't be
sitting here looking so down.

365
00:41:01,760 --> 00:41:03,280
I'd have already thrown a party by now.

366
00:41:08,160 --> 00:41:09,880
I really don't get you.

367
00:41:09,960 --> 00:41:13,160
This is every boxer's ultimate dream.

368
00:41:14,960 --> 00:41:15,920
Yeah, it is.

369
00:41:17,520 --> 00:41:18,360
And?

370
00:41:23,080 --> 00:41:25,720
Forget it. I'm done talking to you.
I'll go work instead.

371
00:41:27,160 --> 00:41:30,200
I ask, and you don't answer.
All you do is sigh.

372
00:41:40,760 --> 00:41:42,520
That way! Hurry!

373
00:42:02,720 --> 00:42:03,960
Those people followed me here.

374
00:42:07,920 --> 00:42:09,160
This way. Come on.

375
00:42:10,120 --> 00:42:11,520
Go after them!

376
00:42:17,240 --> 00:42:18,440
Who is this?

377
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:24,960
I don't know either.

378
00:42:25,040 --> 00:42:26,240
‪What?

379
00:42:33,920 --> 00:42:35,040
Miss.

380
00:42:35,560 --> 00:42:37,440
My name's Haw.

381
00:42:38,080 --> 00:42:39,200
What's yours?

382
00:42:44,880 --> 00:42:47,960
Let me know when you find out.
She doesn't want to talk to me.

383
00:42:49,280 --> 00:42:50,480
Good that you noticed.

384
00:43:03,560 --> 00:43:05,760
Hey, don't you know how to walk?

385
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:09,360
What? First you bumped into me,
and now you do it again.

386
00:43:09,440 --> 00:43:10,840
Keep your voice down.

387
00:43:13,000 --> 00:43:14,080
You can talk now?

388
00:43:32,360 --> 00:43:33,400
Hey!

389
00:43:34,240 --> 00:43:37,440
Are you crazy? Why would you call them?
I'll have to run again if they find me.

390
00:43:38,840 --> 00:43:40,920
Wow, you can really talk.

391
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:42,600
You can say anything except thank you.

392
00:43:48,840 --> 00:43:49,680
Thanks.

393
00:43:52,560 --> 00:43:54,520
- Hey!
- Don't.

394
00:44:01,920 --> 00:44:03,120
Thank you.

395
00:44:04,440 --> 00:44:05,480
That's better.

396
00:44:09,160 --> 00:44:10,080
Wait here.

397
00:44:10,680 --> 00:44:12,440
Once they're gone, I'll come get you.

398
00:44:12,520 --> 00:44:14,320
Haw, I'm leaving her with you.

399
00:44:14,400 --> 00:44:15,480
Nah.

400
00:44:17,920 --> 00:44:20,440
- What if she insults me again?
- Come on.

401
00:44:21,960 --> 00:44:22,800
Fine.

402
00:44:33,920 --> 00:44:35,400
Hey, did you find her?

403
00:44:35,480 --> 00:44:36,680
No, I didn't.

404
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:38,760
Looking for someone?

405
00:44:40,080 --> 00:44:42,040
A woman about this tall.

406
00:44:42,120 --> 00:44:44,120
Long hair, blonde.

407
00:44:45,120 --> 00:44:46,320
No one like that here.

408
00:44:47,080 --> 00:44:50,360
But if you two aren't drinking,
I'll have to ask you to wait outside.

409
00:44:51,040 --> 00:44:52,440
Sorry, guys.

410
00:45:07,320 --> 00:45:08,520
- Dom.
- Huh?

411
00:45:08,600 --> 00:45:10,680
Tell that woman to leave.

412
00:45:10,760 --> 00:45:12,760
We're closed. Dum's gonna get mad.

413
00:45:12,840 --> 00:45:13,840
Yeah.

414
00:45:15,520 --> 00:45:17,640
You should go. We're closed.

415
00:45:27,080 --> 00:45:27,920
Asleep?

416
00:45:31,920 --> 00:45:32,880
Hey.

417
00:45:38,680 --> 00:45:39,840
Hey.

418
00:45:41,440 --> 00:45:42,680
Hey.

419
00:45:46,880 --> 00:45:48,040
Hey.

420
00:45:56,560 --> 00:45:58,400
You need to go home.

421
00:46:04,480 --> 00:46:06,440
I'll help you get a taxi.

422
00:46:06,960 --> 00:46:08,560
Do you remember where you live?

423
00:46:13,440 --> 00:46:14,360
Taxi.

424
00:46:22,160 --> 00:46:23,360
Come on.

425
00:46:29,520 --> 00:46:31,160
Get home safe.

426
00:46:37,720 --> 00:46:38,960
Sukhumvit 55, please.

427
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:07,240
She's pretty, huh?

428
00:47:08,720 --> 00:47:10,040
You think?

429
00:47:12,600 --> 00:47:13,560
You like her?

430
00:47:22,200 --> 00:47:23,760
If you like her, that's better.

431
00:47:24,560 --> 00:47:26,400
I don't want you messing with his woman.

432
00:47:31,080 --> 00:47:34,840
You know that case about Fon's mom
you had me look into,

433
00:47:36,320 --> 00:47:37,840
there's been no progress at all.

434
00:47:38,520 --> 00:47:40,880
Fon said her senior at work
was handling it, right?

435
00:47:40,960 --> 00:47:43,120
- Champ?
- Yeah.

436
00:47:46,040 --> 00:47:48,600
I don't know what the truth is.

437
00:47:49,320 --> 00:47:50,200
But I think Champ

438
00:47:51,120 --> 00:47:53,720
definitely has someone powerful
backing him.

439
00:47:56,480 --> 00:47:57,320
Why's that?

440
00:47:57,400 --> 00:47:59,760
He is in charge of drug cases.

441
00:48:00,600 --> 00:48:03,080
I've seen him lead raids many times,

442
00:48:03,160 --> 00:48:06,520
but he only catches small fish.
Especially in Peng's area,

443
00:48:07,960 --> 00:48:09,320
I've never seen him catch anyone.

444
00:48:11,560 --> 00:48:13,920
Only once in a while
does he seize a big shipment.

445
00:48:14,640 --> 00:48:17,840
You guys are all the same.
Just going along with it.

446
00:48:17,920 --> 00:48:19,400
Not me, Pong.

447
00:48:20,960 --> 00:48:23,400
How many people like him
do you think there are?

448
00:48:26,080 --> 00:48:27,720
At least he has me, doesn't he?

449
00:48:28,320 --> 00:48:30,840
Hey, do you still remember

450
00:48:30,920 --> 00:48:32,640
we agreed not to get involved with drugs?

451
00:48:34,880 --> 00:48:36,120
I remember.

452
00:48:37,400 --> 00:48:39,040
That's why Oab's the odd one out here.

453
00:48:42,040 --> 00:48:45,280
That's why we have no allies.
Everyone wants to get rich quick.

454
00:48:45,360 --> 00:48:48,320
They don't care
how badly society falls apart.

455
00:48:48,400 --> 00:48:49,880
Are we really going to get rich

456
00:48:50,480 --> 00:48:53,040
by standing on the ruins we've created?

457
00:48:53,960 --> 00:48:57,400
How could we face our children
growing up in a society like this?

458
00:48:59,480 --> 00:49:00,560
Right?

459
00:49:09,120 --> 00:49:12,640
With drugs spreading this badly,
why haven't they gotten to Peng yet?

460
00:49:13,520 --> 00:49:14,880
There's no evidence.

461
00:49:14,960 --> 00:49:18,920
Like I told you, the people in charge
aren't taking it seriously.

462
00:49:21,600 --> 00:49:23,360
What if it were me? Would you arrest me?

463
00:49:24,440 --> 00:49:25,280
Yes.

464
00:49:27,200 --> 00:49:29,720
- You wouldn't even spare a friend?
- No.

465
00:49:29,800 --> 00:49:32,360
If you ever sank that low
and started dealing drugs, I'd arrest you.

466
00:49:35,480 --> 00:49:36,280
Oab.

467
00:49:37,520 --> 00:49:39,200
But I know you'd never do that.

468
00:49:42,960 --> 00:49:45,400
What are you two
whispering about over there?

469
00:49:47,680 --> 00:49:50,160
He asked if you liked men.

470
00:49:50,240 --> 00:49:52,680
He said you never look for a wife
and spend all day with him.

471
00:49:52,760 --> 00:49:55,960
- Want me to kick your ass?
- Whoa, Pong.

472
00:49:57,160 --> 00:49:59,960
- Pong, I'm joking.
- Take this.

473
00:50:00,640 --> 00:50:01,920
Hey, Pong.

474
00:50:17,080 --> 00:50:18,680
You're still up, Fon?

475
00:50:20,320 --> 00:50:23,600
- There's something I want to ask you.
- Go ahead.

476
00:50:24,760 --> 00:50:27,920
When I got clipped by that car,
did you know who did it?

477
00:50:29,240 --> 00:50:30,400
Yes.

478
00:50:31,160 --> 00:50:34,840
- Did you send your men to deal with them?
- No.

479
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:38,360
So you didn't know about it?

480
00:50:39,920 --> 00:50:40,840
I knew.

481
00:50:42,480 --> 00:50:44,120
Dom was the one who handled everything.

482
00:50:47,040 --> 00:50:48,120
But you didn't know?

483
00:50:49,360 --> 00:50:50,320
I didn't order it.

484
00:50:51,120 --> 00:50:52,760
But I agree with what he did.

485
00:51:03,160 --> 00:51:04,640
Is that all you wanted to ask me?

486
00:51:08,080 --> 00:51:09,200
Yes?

487
00:51:09,960 --> 00:51:11,360
That's all you wanted to ask me?

488
00:51:13,520 --> 00:51:17,000
I saw the case file, so I wanted to know
if you were the one behind it.

489
00:51:19,600 --> 00:51:20,520
That's all. I'm…

490
00:51:21,680 --> 00:51:23,080
I'm going to bed.

491
00:51:48,040 --> 00:51:50,320
Do you think money can change people?

492
00:51:51,560 --> 00:51:54,360
Of course. If you put a million baht
in front of me right now,

493
00:51:54,440 --> 00:51:55,920
I could become a thief.

494
00:51:57,240 --> 00:51:58,440
I'm being serious.

495
00:51:59,320 --> 00:52:01,480
Come on, I'm just joking.

496
00:52:01,560 --> 00:52:03,920
Why? Is something going on?

497
00:52:05,040 --> 00:52:08,000
Well, a friend of mine
got involved with someone powerful.

498
00:52:09,440 --> 00:52:11,320
He says he wants to quit,

499
00:52:11,920 --> 00:52:13,480
but I don't see him doing it.

500
00:52:14,640 --> 00:52:18,160
When money and power are within reach,
they can't walk away.

501
00:52:19,240 --> 00:52:20,280
Why would you say that?

502
00:52:21,880 --> 00:52:22,960
Was your friend ever poor?

503
00:52:28,880 --> 00:52:31,240
Was he ever looked down on?

504
00:52:35,880 --> 00:52:38,760
Did he ever say
he wanted more than he had,

505
00:52:38,840 --> 00:52:39,960
just to prove them wrong?

506
00:52:45,640 --> 00:52:47,480
Then he'll never quit.

507
00:52:47,560 --> 00:52:51,360
If his life got better,
even if it meant doing wrong,

508
00:52:51,440 --> 00:52:53,440
I think he'd accept it.

509
00:52:58,520 --> 00:53:01,080
Fon, the chief wants to see you.

510
00:53:01,160 --> 00:53:02,240
Okay.

511
00:53:04,320 --> 00:53:05,440
- I'll be back.
- Yeah.

512
00:53:11,720 --> 00:53:13,320
POL. MAJ. GEN. SAENCHAI SAENSUWAN

513
00:53:16,000 --> 00:53:17,640
He doesn't listen to a word I say.

514
00:53:19,160 --> 00:53:22,200
If I were him,
I wouldn't let Dom quit either.

515
00:53:25,280 --> 00:53:27,680
Dom is the only one
who's gotten this close to Oab.

516
00:53:29,920 --> 00:53:32,880
He's gotten so close that even I can tell
he's not the same anymore.

517
00:53:34,600 --> 00:53:36,800
I'm afraid that if this keeps going,

518
00:53:36,880 --> 00:53:39,080
he will become someone I don't know.

519
00:53:47,800 --> 00:53:51,240
If he can't back out, I think

520
00:53:51,920 --> 00:53:53,560
we should bring this to an end.

521
00:54:14,920 --> 00:54:16,600
- Dom.
- What?

522
00:54:16,680 --> 00:54:19,040
Hey, you're done training already?

523
00:54:19,120 --> 00:54:20,240
Yeah.

524
00:54:21,440 --> 00:54:24,080
After training,

525
00:54:24,600 --> 00:54:26,440
you gotta go somewhere with him?

526
00:54:26,520 --> 00:54:27,760
I've got something to do.

527
00:54:29,760 --> 00:54:31,360
After that,

528
00:54:32,800 --> 00:54:34,080
you coming to the bar?

529
00:54:34,160 --> 00:54:35,600
You want me to help out?

530
00:54:35,680 --> 00:54:36,880
Yeah.

531
00:54:37,800 --> 00:54:39,240
You free?

532
00:54:40,800 --> 00:54:42,160
Come help me.

533
00:54:42,680 --> 00:54:45,640
Ever since you started training,
I've been working my ass off.

534
00:54:46,440 --> 00:54:49,680
Dum's handling the gambling den,
so I'm running the place alone.

535
00:54:49,760 --> 00:54:53,400
Hey, stop complaining.
Whatever he asks you to do, just do it.

536
00:54:55,000 --> 00:54:58,160
I signed up to be a boxer. Look at me now.

537
00:54:58,240 --> 00:55:01,800
I'm mopping floors and washing dishes.

538
00:55:03,800 --> 00:55:05,200
How about this?

539
00:55:06,480 --> 00:55:09,200
After work tonight, train with me.

540
00:55:09,800 --> 00:55:11,840
Hey, you said it.

541
00:55:16,280 --> 00:55:18,200
Why is there so much this time?

542
00:55:19,040 --> 00:55:22,200
I'm working on a new deal,
so I need to keep some ready for them.

543
00:55:25,080 --> 00:55:26,320
Okay.

544
00:55:26,400 --> 00:55:29,960
Keep it here for now.
If I need it, I'll come get it.

545
00:55:31,440 --> 00:55:32,480
Sure.

546
00:55:35,680 --> 00:55:37,120
Hurry and put it away upstairs.

547
00:55:38,800 --> 00:55:39,640
Careful.

548
00:55:57,840 --> 00:55:59,560
Why do you keep coming here so often?

549
00:56:02,080 --> 00:56:03,040
I need to talk to you.

550
00:56:06,080 --> 00:56:07,040
About what?

551
00:56:08,600 --> 00:56:09,880
Are you sure?

552
00:56:09,960 --> 00:56:12,760
If I wasn't sure,
I wouldn't have come here myself.

553
00:56:12,840 --> 00:56:14,760
But Peng's men are all over the arena.

554
00:56:15,400 --> 00:56:17,120
I've got just as many men as he does.

555
00:56:17,200 --> 00:56:19,360
Oab, from what I've heard,

556
00:56:19,440 --> 00:56:22,200
there's no chance
we'll make it back alive.

557
00:56:27,320 --> 00:56:28,680
That's my problem.

558
00:56:30,560 --> 00:56:32,920
Your only job is to step into that ring

559
00:56:33,000 --> 00:56:35,600
and bring that belt back to me.

560
00:56:39,120 --> 00:56:42,520
Don't worry. I'm not that easy to kill.

561
00:57:18,400 --> 00:57:21,200
I shouldn't have trusted you, Dom.

562
00:57:24,720 --> 00:57:25,480
Pong.

563
00:57:25,560 --> 00:57:26,760
What are you doing?

564
00:57:26,840 --> 00:57:27,840
<i>Dum, help!</i>

565
00:57:27,920 --> 00:57:29,320
Are you handling this case?

566
00:57:29,400 --> 00:57:30,640
I worked on this case before.

567
00:57:30,720 --> 00:57:33,840
Do you remember
who was in charge of this case?

568
00:57:33,920 --> 00:57:36,200
Especially now,
they probably want to close the case.

569
00:57:36,280 --> 00:57:38,320
They'll likely do what we ask.

570
00:57:39,040 --> 00:57:41,160
You're no fun to drink with.

571
00:57:41,240 --> 00:57:43,480
If you're not having fun,
I suggest you go to another bar.

572
00:57:55,840 --> 00:57:57,680
I really love you, Fon.

573
00:57:59,320 --> 00:58:00,880
Let's get back together.

574
00:58:43,600 --> 00:58:45,520
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
